# Rules for apex unit tests
Follow the guidelines below:
- Unit Test Classes should named like "Test_<ClassName>" ,for example: Test_AccountHelper.
- Test methods naming convention should be in the format "whatShouldWhen".
- Avoid hardcoding ids.
- Avoid data creation and queries when applicable.
- Avoid using @seeAllData annotation.
- Use the [SObjectBuilder.cls](mdc:src/classes/SObjectBuilder.cls) and [SObjectFactory.cls](mdc:src/classes/SObjectFactory.cls) for the data creation in the unit tests. - Use setFields or setFields methods to populate the fields.
- Test classes and methods must be private.
- Use the @testSetup annotation when applicable. Method should be called testData.
- Use @isTest annotation instead of testmethod keyword.
- No test methods without asserts.
- Always use assert message.
- It is also recommended to always use Test.startTest and Test.stopTest to determine what is actually being tested, the inner block should have an indentation of 4 spaces.
- Use [ValueProvider.cls](mdc:src/classes/ValueProvider.cls) to create a fields values.
- Generate cls-meta.xml file with the current API version.
- Use string variables for the assert messages and field values. 